      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina looked at the fox, wondering what sorrow made his voice so brittle. She realized he wasn't just being mean; he was protecting something he feared to lose. She reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, setting it on the step between them. This is for the trouble of walking me down, she said softly."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his gaze softening as if he were remembering a distant autumn. He finally stood up, adjusted his patched green vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. He beckoned for Lina to follow, his movements slow and careful as they descended into the quiet dark."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
